BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-194588@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260721T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260721T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260721T213000
SUMMARY:Private Screening: "The Odyssey" 
LOCATION:Offsite: Alamo Drafthouse Seaport
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are Con
 firmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194588\n\n6:00P
 M Doors Open\, 6:30PM - 9:30PM Screening\nJoin us for a ‘Quin-exclusive 
 private screening of Christopher Nolan’s highly anticipated adaptation o
 f The Odyssey.\n\nA sweeping mythological epic inspired by Homer's timeles
 s poem\, The Odyssey stars Matt Damon as Odysseus\, the legendary King of 
 Ithaca. The film chronicles his perilous decade-long journey home followin
 g the Trojan War\, where he encounters mythical creatures\, vengeful gods\
 , and extraordinary trials in his relentless quest to reunite with his wif
 e\, Penelope. An evening of epic storytelling awaits...\n\n*This event is 
 complimentary and reserved for members\, plus one registered guest. Tables
 ide food and beverage service is available in the theater.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194588
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-192746@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260722T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T190000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Decisions That Changed the World
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are
  Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192746\n\n5
 :30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion \nAs the United States celebrates its
  250th anniversary\, join us for a timely conversation examining the decis
 ions that have shaped America's role in the world. Drawing on a landmark 2
 026 survey conducted by the Council on Foreign Relations and the Society f
 or Historians of American Foreign Relations\, James M. Lindsay\, distingui
 shed senior fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations\, will be joined by
  Mary Yntema\, past President & CEO of WorldBoston\, a World Affairs Counc
 il\, and governance and strategy consultant\, to explore the ten most cons
 equential successes—and failures—in U.S. foreign policy since the nati
 on's founding.\n\nThrough the lenses of history\, strategy\, and democrati
 c values\, this discussion will consider what these pivotal choices reveal
  about American leadership\, global engagement\, and the challenges that l
 ie ahead. At a moment when the international order is once again being red
 efined\, this promises to be a thought-provoking exploration of how the pa
 st informs the future.\n\nMembers will also receive a copy of the survey's
  foreign policy scorecard\, providing an opportunity to weigh in on the ra
 nkings and continue the conversation with fellow attendees following the d
 iscussion.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members\, plus
  one guest. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192746
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-195310@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260723T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T200000
SUMMARY:Member Mixer: The Story Behind It
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Member Mixer\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 21 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1
 95310\n\nEvery cherished object carries a story.\n\nJoin fellow members fo
 r an intimate evening of conversation and discovery as we explore the pers
 onal stories behind life's most meaningful keepsakes. Whether it is a trea
 sured family heirloom\, a memorable travel find\, a piece of art\, a colle
 ctible\, or another object of personal significance\, each item offers a u
 nique glimpse into the experiences\, traditions\, and moments that have sh
 aped its owner.\n\nMembers who wish to participate will be invited to shar
 e their selected piece and its story in a brief presentation\, creating an
  engaging exchange of memories\, history\, and inspiration.\n\n*This event
  is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites
  will be served with beverages available for purchase.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195310
CATEGORIES:Member Mixer
END:VEVENT
