BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-195311@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260804T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T203000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Summer of Love" with Kerri Maher
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 2 spots left\nSt
 atus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195311
 \n\nBookmark the date for an inspiring conversation exploring “The Summe
 r of Love” with author Kerri Maher. Moderated by Wendy Dodson\, owner of
  Humming Bird Books.\n\nSettle into the sand this month and let the Califo
 rnia coast carry you away. A story of family\, love\, ambition\, and long-
 buried secrets\, this is the perfect escape to pack in your beach bag this
  summer. Travel back to the Summer of Love in 1967\, where two sisters fin
 d themselves on very different paths. Winnie dreams of changing the world 
 through poetry in the heart of San Francisco's counterculture\, while Mira
 nda stays home to build her family's California vineyard into something ex
 traordinary.\n\nFifty years later\, Dawn Hartley is pulled back into her f
 amily's past when she sets out to uncover the identity of a mysterious bes
 tselling author who seems to know all of the Hartleys' deepest secrets—i
 ncluding one Dawn is hiding herself.\n\n*This event is complimentary and r
 eserved for members only. Light refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195311
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-194363@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260805T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T210000
SUMMARY:Live Music: Anibal Cruz
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Available\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194363\n\nStep into The
  Reading Room for an unforgettable night of Latin jazz with Cuban pianist\
 , composer\, and bandleader Anibal Cruz. Known for his magnetic blend of C
 uban rhythms and jazz innovation\, Cruz has captivated audiences worldwide
 \, performing alongside icons like Paquito de Rivera and leading his own e
 nsembles\, Clave & Blues and The Blue Island Project. His set will take yo
